---
// Beat 3 · the promise, as one picture of the reader's week.
---

<section id="after" class="py-10 md:py-16 px-6 relative scroll-mt-14">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="absolute -bottom-1/4 -left-1/4 w-[800px] h-[700px] rounded-full opacity-[0.12]"
         style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #89b4fa 0%, transparent 70%);"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="continuum-rule max-w-7xl mx-auto absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-full"></div>
  <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <span class="eyebrow mb-4 block" style="color: #89b4fa;">Monday, after</span>
    <h2 class="text-[1.875rem] md:text-[2.5rem] max-w-[680px] mb-8">
      The thread lands at 9:10. By Thursday, three of four are merged.
    </h2>

    <div class="glass-pane p-6 md:p-8 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-[#f9e2af] mb-2">Mon 09:10</div>
        <p class="text-[0.875rem] text-text-secondary">You paste the Slack thread and close the lid. It lands in an inbox that owes you nothing.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-[#89dceb] mb-2">Mon 10:30 · stand-up</div>
        <p class="text-[0.875rem] text-text-secondary">It is four tasks now, each with acceptance criteria and an order. One carries a question: split auth into two tasks, or keep one? You answer in a line, from your phone.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-[#d4af37] mb-2">Thu 18:04</div>
        <p class="text-[0.875rem] text-text-secondary">Three are on origin, checked by sha. The fourth is waiting on a fact only you know. Nobody opened a session by hand.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 text-[0.875rem] text-text-muted max-w-[640px]">
      The typing goes to the agents. What stays with you is judgment: is this in scope,
      is this true, should this reach the outside world.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
